cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "PetzCurvature: a Lean 4 proof of Petz's conjecture for the Kubo–Mori metric"
authors:
  - family-names: Bornemann
    given-names: Adam
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24460110
repository-code: "https://github.com/Charmooo/PetzCurvature"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A formal proof, in Lean 4 with Mathlib, of Petz's conjecture (Conjecture 6.3 of
  D. Petz, J. Math. Phys. 35 (1994)) that the scalar curvature of the
  Bogoliubov–Kubo–Mori metric on the faithful density matrices of any size is
  monotone under mixing: if the eigenvalues of one state are majorized by those of
  another, its scalar curvature is at least as large. The proof follows Dittmann
  (Linear Algebra Appl. 315 (2000)): it formalizes his closed form for the scalar
  curvature as a sum over triples of eigenvalues (Theorem 2) and his reduction of
  the conjecture to four inequalities (Theorem 3), and proves those inequalities,
  which Dittmann had checked only numerically, with kernel-checked sign
  certificates for exponential polynomials. Also proved are the strict form for
  states with different spectra, the value (n² − 1)(n² − 4)/8 at the trace state
  and its maximality, and Petz's condition that the scalar curvature of a Gibbs
  state increases with the temperature.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - quantum information geometry
  - monotone metrics
  - Kubo–Mori metric
  - Bogoliubov–Kubo–Mori metric
  - scalar curvature
  - majorization
  - Petz conjecture
